---
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>My Graphic Design Portfolio</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem;
      background-color: #ffffff;
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }
    h1 { 
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .hero {
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }
    .hero p {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: #444;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .cta-link {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 1rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
      background-color: #1a1a1a;
      color: #ffffff;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 4px;
      font-weight: 600;
      transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
    }
    .cta-link:hover {
      background-color: #444444;
    }
    .project-section {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
    }
    .project-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.8rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <Navigation />

  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Designing for people.</h1>
    <p>I'm Kristen, a graphic designer specializing in web design, UX/UI, and accessibility. I create digital experiences that look and feel good.</p>
    <a href="/portfolio/work/" class="cta-link">View My Work →</a>
    <a href="/portfolio/about/" class="cta-link">More About Me →</a>
  </header>

<!-- Section 1: Intro / What I Do -->
<section class="intro-section">
  <h2>Good design should work for everyone.</h2>
  <p>Accessibility isn’t something I add at the end of a project. It’s part of my approach from the beginning. Whether I’m building a website, developing a brand, or even just picking a font, I’m always thinking about how someone will actually experience it.</p>
</section>

<!-- Section 2: Specialties -->
<section class="specialties-section">
  <h2>What I do</h2>
  <h3>Web Design</h3>
  <p>Websites designed to be easy to navigate, engaging, and accessible across devices.</p>
  <h3>UX / UI</h3>
  <p>Turning ideas into digital experiences. I focus on clear structure, intuitive interactions, and user-centered design.</p>
  <h3>Accessibility</h3>
  <p>Designing for all. From visual hierarchy and color contrast to navigation, interaction, and content, I consider accessibility throughout the process.</p>
  <h3>Graphic Design</h3>
  <p>Brand identities, visual systems, and everything in between. I like making things look good and making sure they look that way for a reason.</p>
</section>

<!-- Section 3: Featured Work -->
<section class="featured-section">
  <h2>A few things I’ve made</h2>
  <p>A collection of websites, identities, and interactive experiences created with exploration, intention, and probably way too many tabs open.</p>
  <a href="/portfolio/work/" class="cta-link">See All Work →</a>
</section>

<!-- Section 4: Closing CTA -->
<section class="closing-section">
  <h2>Let’s make something that works.</h2>
  <p>Have a project, opportunity, or idea? I’d love to hear about it.</p>
  <a href="/portfolio/contact/" class="cta-link">Get in Touch →</a>

</body>
</html>
